                  "title": "Easy Steam Chicken - COOK.ME",
                  "url": "https://cook.me/recipe/easy-steam-chicken/?utm_source=valyu.ai&utm_medium=referral",
                  "content": "# Easy Steam Chicken\n\n## Your favorite way to cook chicken\n\n## Ingredients\n\n## Nutritional Information\n\nFragrant, garlicky and coated in a yummy Asian sauce, this Steam Chicken is one of my favorite ways to cook chicken. Steaming chicken breasts is certainly not a common method for cooking them but it’s done a lot in Asian cuisine as it keeps the chicken amazingly moist and juicy. And if you really want to be authentic you can even add some aromatics, such as lemongrass, to the boiling water to infuse the chicken with extra flavor!\n\nMy recipe takes the extra step of covering the chicken with salt before steaming. Even though you wash the salt off I think it adds a good deal of extra flavor. If you’re looking for a recipe to tell you how to steam chicken, I would really recommend giving this delicious version a try!\n\n## How to Steam Chicken\n\nPlace a steamer basket or pan over a pot of boiling water. Add the chicken fillets to the steamer and cover with a lid. Steam the chicken for about 30 minutes or until the juices run clear when tested. For added flavor, you can add aromatics like lemongrass, garlic, or ginger to the boiling water. If you’re wondering how to steam chicken for the best results, this method keeps the meat tender, juicy, and full of natural flavor.\n\nTo make Easy Steam Chicken Recipe, you will need the following ingredients:\n\n### Recipe Features\n\n### Cuisine\n\n## Steps to make\n\n- 1 Salt the chicken 30 min In a medium-sized bowl, pour the cup of salt over the chicken. Rub the salt into the fillets and place in the refrigerator for half an hour.\n\n### Salt the chicken\n\nIn a medium-sized bowl, pour the cup of salt over the chicken. Rub the salt into the fillets and place in the refrigerator for half an hour.\n\n- 2 Clean the chicken 1 min Rinse the fillets thoroughly under running water until all the salt has been removed.\n\n### Clean the chicken\n\nRinse the fillets thoroughly under running water until all the salt has been removed.\n\n- 3 Steam the chicken 30 min Place a steamer basket or pan over a pot of boiling water. Add the fillets to the steamer and cook for about 30 minutes, until the chicken juices run clear when tested.\n\n### Steam the chicken\n\nPlace a steamer basket or pan over a pot of boiling water. Add the fillets to the steamer and cook for about 30 minutes, until the chicken juices run clear when tested.\n\n- 4 Cook the onion 5 min Place a pan over a medium heat and add the vegetable oil. Once hot, add the onion and cook for 3-5 minutes until translucent.\n\n### Cook the onion\n\nPlace a pan over a medium heat and add the vegetable oil. Once hot, add the onion and cook for 3-5 minutes until translucent.\n\n- 5 Cook the garlic 2 min Add the garlic and fry for another minute, stirring regularly.\n\n### Cook the garlic\n\nAdd the garlic and fry for another minute, stirring regularly.\n\n- 6 Add the sauces 2 min Pour in the soy sauce and sesame oil and toss to coat.\n\n### Add the sauces\n\nPour in the soy sauce and sesame oil and toss to coat.\n\n- 7 Serving Steamed Asian Chicken 5 min Place the cooked fillets on a plate. Ladle the onion sauce over them and scatter the cilantro leaves on top.\n\n### Serving Steamed Asian Chicken\n\nPlace the cooked fillets on a plate. Ladle the onion sauce over them and scatter the cilantro leaves on top.\n\nThis Steamed Asian Chicken is so yummy served with the sauce ladled over the top and accompanied by a big bowl of fragrant rice. Get your chopsticks ready! If you have a go at this recipe why not take a snap and share it with me - just tag #cookmerecipes!\n\n## About the author\n\n### Bethany Lim\n\n## Recipe Reviews\n\nHave you made this recipe? Share your experience and help other cooks!\n\n### Detailed Recipe Rating\n\n#### Rating Distribution\n\nThanks!\n\n## Related Recipes\n\n### Categories:\n\n### Main Ingredients:\n\n### Tomato Chicken Skillet\n\n### Chicken Francese\n\n### Chicken Schnitzel\n\n### Shredded Chicken Tacos\n\n### The Original Marry Me Chicken Recipe\n\n### Breaded Chicken No Egg\n\n### Fresh & Healthy Avocado Cauliflower Rice\n\n### Roasted Hispi Cabbage with Garlic Tahini Sauce\n\n### Creamy Garlic Skillet Chicken with Spinach\n\n### Maroulosalata (Greek Lettuce Salad)\n\n### Recipe Navigation\n\n#### Jump to Section\n\n- Back to Top\n\n- Ingredients\n\n- Nutrition Facts\n\n- Instructions\n\n- Step by Step\n\n- Reviews\n\n- Related Recipes",
